{# ─── LOCAL CONTEXT: what makes Trinity Beach different ─── #}
<section class="copy-block">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <span class="eyebrow">House Painter Trinity Beach</span>
    <h2>What painting in Trinity Beach actually involves</h2>
    <p style="margin-top:14px">Trinity Beach sits on the northern Cairns coast, postcode 4879 — about 20 minutes north of the CBD, wedged between Clifton Beach and Kewarra. Most of the housing stock is from the 90s and 2000s: rendered brick, lightweight cladding, plenty of tile roofs. Beautiful spot to live, hard on paint.</p>
    <p style="margin-top:14px">Here's what we see on nearly every Trinity Beach repaint:</p>

    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px;margin-top:20px">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:17px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:700">Salt creep</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55">The ocean's a kilometre away. Salt mist eats coatings, especially on the windward side of the house.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:17px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:700">Wet season blowouts</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55">Dec–Mar humidity opens up hairline cracks in render, blisters cheap exterior paint, and feeds mould on the south side.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:17px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:700">UV scorch on north-facing walls</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55">Tropical sun hammers anything not finished in a quality UV-stable coating. Cheap paint goes chalky in 18 months.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--rule);border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;font-size:17px;color:var(--ink);font-weight:700">Soft timber around eaves and fascia</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55">Once moisture's in, prep is everything — patch-and-paint over rotten timber is a 12-month fix at best.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p style="margin-top:24px">Most Trinity Beach houses need a full exterior repaint every 5 to 7 years to keep the seal tight. We use exterior systems built for coastal tropical conditions — Dulux Weathershield, Solver Aquashield, and Sikkens for timber — and we don't cut corners on prep. If a board's gone soft, we replace it before we paint.</p>
  </div>
</section>

